---
const LEAD_ENDPOINT = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_LEAD_ENDPOINT || "https://admin.deleadint.com/api/lead";
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Walk2Lead Robotics Tech Quest | Implemented by De' Lead International</title>
<meta name="description" content="44 government schools. 1,300+ children. Walk2Lead is funded by Walkaroo Foundation and implemented end-to-end by De' Lead International, a prominent CSR implementation team. See the numbers, the setbacks, and how we solved them.">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Lora:ital,wght@0,500;0,600;0,700;1,500;1,600&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/styles.css">
</head>
<body>

<nav id="nav">
  <div class="wrap nav-inner">
    <a class="nav-logo" href="#top"><img class="logo-color" src="/assets/walk2lead-logo.svg" alt="Walk2Lead"><img class="logo-white" src="/assets/walk2lead-logo-white.svg" alt="Walk2Lead"></a>
    <ul class="nav-links">
      <li><a href="#story">Story</a></li>
      <li><a href="#impact">Impact</a></li>
      <li><a href="#reality">How We Deliver</a></li>
      <li><a href="#voices">Voices</a></li>
      <li><a href="#gallery">Gallery</a></li>
      <li class="nav-cta-li"><a class="btn btn-primary nav-cta" href="#partner">Partner With Us</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</nav>

<!-- HERO — bento -->
<header class="hero" id="top">
  <div class="wrap bento">
    <div class="b-head reveal">
      <svg class="doodle-spark d1" viewBox="0 0 60 60" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M30 4 C33 20 40 27 56 30 C40 33 33 40 30 56 C27 40 20 33 4 30 C20 27 27 20 30 4 Z" stroke="var(--red-bright)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      <svg class="doodle-spark d2" viewBox="0 0 60 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 12 C10 3 16 3 22 12 C28 21 34 21 40 12 C46 3 52 3 58 12" stroke="var(--magenta)" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
      <div class="b-live reveal"><span class="dot"></span> Phase 4 running now in Kozhikode, Malappuram &amp; Wayanad</div>
      <h1>44 government schools. <span class="doodle-wrap"><mark>1,300+</mark><svg class="doodle-circle" viewBox="0 0 200 90" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14,42 C10,14 58,2 101,4 C152,6 197,17 191,47 C186,76 129,87 89,84 C38,81 19,73 14,42 Z" stroke="var(--red)" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg></span> children. Robots that actually worked.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Walk2Lead Robotics Tech Quest brings hands-on robotics, coding and AI into rural government schools across Kerala, funded by Walkaroo Foundation and implemented end-to-end by <strong>De' Lead International</strong>, a prominent CSR implementation team. In association with the District Institutes of Education and Training (DIET) and the General Education Department, Government of Kerala. Four phases. Scaling every time.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions" style="display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-start">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#partner">Start a CSR project →</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#reality">See how we deliver</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="b-photo-group reveal">
      <div class="hero-slides">
        <!-- ADD MORE GROUP PHOTOS HERE — duplicate a <div class="hero-slide"> block -->
        <div class="hero-slide"><img src="/assets/big-group.jpg" alt="Walk2Lead cohort group photo"></div>
        <div class="hero-slide"><img src="/assets/group-hall-wyd.jpg" alt="Walk2Lead Wayanad cohort group photo" style="object-position:center bottom"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="b-actions reveal">
      <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="b-actions-logo" src="/assets/logo-delead-dark.png" alt="De' Lead International" style="width:auto;object-fit:contain">
      <div class="b-actions-text">
        <div class="b-actions-title">Implemented by De' Lead International</div>
        <p class="b-actions-sub">India &amp; UAE · "Learn, Develop &amp; Lead"</p>
      </div>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#delead">Why us →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <svg class="hero-wave" viewBox="0 0 1440 90" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M0,32 C240,80 480,0 720,28 C960,56 1200,88 1440,40 L1440,90 L0,90 Z" fill="var(--ink)"/></svg>
</header>

<div class="marquee">
  <div class="marquee-track">
    <span>Robotics</span><span>Arduino</span><span>Sensors</span><span>AI-Assisted Coding</span><span>Design Thinking</span><span>School Expos</span><span>District Innovators Expo</span>
    <span>Robotics</span><span>Arduino</span><span>Sensors</span><span>AI-Assisted Coding</span><span>Design Thinking</span><span>School Expos</span><span>District Innovators Expo</span>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- TRUST STRIP -->
<div class="trust reveal">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="trust-lead">
      <span>Implemented by</span>
      <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/logo-delead-dark.png" alt="De' Lead International">
    </div>
    <div class="trust-partners">
      <div class="trust-funder">
        <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/logo-walkaroo.jpg" alt="Walkaroo Foundation">
      </div>
      <div class="trust-diets">
        <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/logo-diet-mlp.jpg" alt="DIET Malappuram">
        <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/logo-diet-kkd.png" alt="DIET Kozhikode">
        <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/logo-diet-knr.jpg" alt="DIET Kannur">
        <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/logo-diet-wyd.jpg" alt="DIET Wayanad">
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ABOUT / PROGRAM -->
<section id="program">
  <div class="wrap about-grid">
    <div class="reveal">
      <div class="eyebrow">The Programme</div>
      <h2 class="h2">A 3-month journey from curiosity to a working robot</h2>
      <p class="lead">Walk2Lead Robotics Tech Quest is a three-month, activity-based programme for Classes 6 &amp; 7 in government schools, reaching children in rural and coastal communities who rarely get access to STEM education of this quality.</p>
      <div class="about-points">
        <div class="point"><div class="ico"><svg class="ico-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="width:22px;height:22px" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"></circle><path d="M19.4 15a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 .33 1.82l.06.06a2 2 0 1 1-2.83 2.83l-.06-.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.82-.33 1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1 1.51V21a2 2 0 0 1-4 0v-.09A1.65 1.65 0 0 0 9 19.4a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.82.33l-.06.06a2 2 0 1 1-2.83-2.83l.06-.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 .33-1.82 1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.51-1H3a2 2 0 0 1 0-4h.09A1.65 1.65 0 0 0 4.6 9a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-.33-1.82l-.06-.06a2 2 0 1 1 2.83-2.83l.06.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.82.33H9a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1-1.51V3a2 2 0 0 1 4 0v.09a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1 1.51 1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.82-.33l.06-.06a2 2 0 1 1 2.83 2.83l-.06.06a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-.33 1.82V9a1.65 1.65 0 0 0 1.51 1H21a2 2 0 0 1 0 4h-.09a1.65 1.65 0 0 0-1.51 1z"></path></svg></div><div><b>30 sessions per school: 26 hands-on, 4 presentation</b><p>Electronics, Arduino, sensors, coding fundamentals and AI-assisted building across 26 hands-on sessions, plus 4 dedicated presentation sessions, with every student prototyping on real kits, not slides.</p></div></div>
        <div class="point"><div class="ico"><svg class="ico-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="width:22px;height:22px" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"></circle><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2"></circle></svg></div><div><b>Two-stage merit selection</b><p>An orientation ideathon, then a school-conducted written aptitude test, selects ~30 students per school from cohorts of 300–400 applicants.</p></div></div>
        <div class="point"><div class="ico"><svg class="ico-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="width:22px;height:22px" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="8" r="7"></circle><polyline points="8.21 13.89 7 23 12 20 17 23 15.79 13.88"></polyline></svg></div><div><b>School expos → District Innovators Expo</b><p>Every phase ends with students pitching working prototypes to an external jury of technologists and educators.</p></div></div>
        <div class="point"><div class="ico"><svg class="ico-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="width:22px;height:22px" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="18" y1="20" x2="18" y2="10"></line><line x1="12" y1="20" x2="12" y2="4"></line><line x1="6" y1="20" x2="6" y2="14"></line></svg></div><div><b>Real-time transparency portal</b><p>De' Lead tracks session progress, attendance and school-wise detail live on the Walk2Lead portal, giving Walkaroo Foundation full visibility and board-ready reporting.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="about-media reveal">
      <img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/kids-building.jpg" alt="Students building their robotics project together">
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="dev-grid reveal">
      <div class="dev-card">
        <h3>Development in STEM Learning</h3>
        <p>Electronics, Arduino, sensors, coding fundamentals and AI-assisted building, taken from first principles to a working prototype every student can demo.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="dev-card">
        <h3>Soft Skill Enrichment</h3>
        <p>Built into the curriculum, not bolted on: every cohort practices these on stage, at the school and district expos.</p>
        <div class="dev-tags"><span>Presentation</span><span>Leadership</span><span>Team Building</span><span>Problem Solving</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- STORY -->
<section class="story" id="story">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow reveal">The Story</div>
    <h2 class="h2 reveal">One school in Kozhikode. Scaled to four districts</h2>
    <p class="lead reveal">Kinalur GUPS was a single pilot in 2023. Walk2Lead has since reached Kozhikode, Malappuram, Wayanad and Kannur, expanding with every phase.</p>
    <div class="story-scatter" id="story-scatter">
      <div class="scatter-photo" style="top:140px;left:40px;--r:-6deg;--d:0s;z-index:1"><img src="/assets/boy-mic.jpg" alt="Student presenting his project" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
      <div class="scatter-photo" style="top:255px;left:250px;--r:5deg;--d:.5s;z-index:2"><img src="/assets/girl-mic-team.jpg" alt="Student team presenting" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
      <div class="scatter-photo" style="top:370px;left:60px;--r:4deg;--d:1s;z-index:3"><img src="/assets/award-kids.jpg" alt="Students receiving recognition" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
      <div class="scatter-photo" style="top:485px;left:240px;--r:-4deg;--d:1.5s;z-index:4"><img src="/assets/panel.jpg" alt="Stakeholder panel at district event" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
      <div class="scatter-photo" style="top:600px;left:50px;--r:7deg;--d:2s;z-index:5"><img src="/assets/memento-group.jpg" alt="Memento distribution ceremony" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
      <div class="scatter-photo" style="top:715px;left:230px;--r:-8deg;--d:2.5s;z-index:6"><img src="/assets/inauguration.jpg" alt="Programme inauguration" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
      <div class="scatter-photo" style="top:830px;left:90px;--r:6deg;--d:3s;z-index:7"><img src="/assets/project-table.jpg" alt="Students demonstrating a prototype" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
      <div class="scatter-photo" style="top:930px;left:260px;--r:-5deg;--d:3.5s;z-index:8"><img src="/assets/expo-team1.jpg" alt="Team at the expo" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="story-line">
      <div class="beat reveal">
        <div class="tag">2023 · Phase 1</div>
        <div class="yr">Kinalur GUPS, Kozhikode</div>
        <h3>The pilot nobody had to renew</h3>
        <p>One school, 48 students, no track record to point to. De' Lead ran the full 30-session curriculum anyway, taking students from electronics to a working prototype, presented by 12-year-olds. It was enough to take the programme into a second district next.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="beat reveal">
        <div class="tag">Phase 2 · Scale-up</div>
        <div class="yr">Malappuram &amp; Kozhikode</div>
        <h3>16 schools, 480 students: the first real test of the system</h3>
        <p>Two districts at once meant real operational strain: shared laptops, patchy power, schools running in parallel across both. The programme still delivered a documented <strong>92.99% average attendance</strong>, tracked school-by-school, not estimated.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="beat reveal">
        <div class="tag">Phase 3 · New ground</div>
        <div class="yr">Kannur</div>
        <h3>Trusted across a third district</h3>
        <p>3 schools, 90 students, including DIET's own Lab School in Palayad, with the academic partner trusting the programme inside its own training ground.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="beat reveal">
        <div class="tag">Phase 4 · Running now</div>
        <div class="yr">Kozhikode, Malappuram &amp; Wayanad</div>
        <h3>24 schools, 705 students, and a jump to the international stage</h3>
        <p>The largest phase yet. Twelve students from this cohort were selected for the <strong>TechTop 2025 International Inclusive Innovation Challenge &amp; Zero2Entrepreneur Bootcamp</strong>, held 28 Nov–4 Dec 2025 at Maker Village, Kochi: 5 from Kozhikode, 7 from Malappuram. Government-school kids from Phase 4, on a global startup stage.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="beat reveal">
        <div class="tag tag-global">28 Nov–4 Dec 2025 · International milestone</div>
        <div class="yr">TechTop 2025 International Inclusive Innovation Challenge &amp; Zero2Entrepreneur Bootcamp</div>
        <h3>Walk2Lead students ranked top 2 — out of the world</h3>
        <p>A 7-day maker-to-entrepreneur bootcamp at <strong>Maker Village, Kochi</strong>, bringing together 37–45 hand-picked student innovators from Grades 6–12 across India, Japan and UAE. Students worked alongside mentors from <strong>MIT and Stanford</strong>, building prototypes addressing UN Sustainable Development Goals. Out of all participants across every country, the <strong>top 2 ranked students came from Walk2Lead</strong> — government school kids from Kerala.</p>
        <div class="z2e-countries">
          <span>🇮🇳 India</span><span>🇯🇵 Japan</span><span>🇦🇪 UAE</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- PHASES -->
<section class="phases" id="phases">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow reveal">By The Numbers</div>
    <h2 class="h2 reveal">Every phase, funded on the results of the last</h2>
    <p class="lead reveal">The strongest endorsement a CSR programme can earn: the same funder, paying for it four times running.</p>
    <div class="timeline">
      <div class="phase reveal"><div class="tag">Phase 1 · Pilot</div><h3>Kinalur GUPS</h3><div class="where">Kozhikode, where it all began</div><div class="stats"><div><b>1</b><span>School</span></div><div><b>48</b><span>Students</span></div></div></div>
      <div class="phase reveal"><div class="tag">Phase 2 · Scale-up</div><h3>Two Districts</h3><div class="where">Malappuram &amp; Kozhikode</div><div class="stats"><div><b>16</b><span>Schools</span></div><div><b>480</b><span>Students</span></div></div></div>
      <div class="phase reveal"><div class="tag">Phase 3 · New Ground</div><h3>Kannur</h3><div class="where">Incl. DIET Lab School, Palayad</div><div class="stats"><div><b>3</b><span>Schools</span></div><div><b>90</b><span>Students</span></div></div></div>
      <div class="phase current reveal"><div class="tag"><span class="live-dot"></span> Phase 4 · Running Now</div><h3>Three Districts</h3><div class="where">Kozhikode, Malappuram &amp; Wayanad</div><div class="stats"><div><b>24</b><span>Schools</span></div><div><b>705</b><span>Students</span></div></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- IMPACT MOSAIC -->
<section class="impact" id="impact">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow reveal">The Numbers</div>
    <h2 class="h2 reveal">What four phases add up to</h2>
    <p class="lead reveal">Not vanity metrics: every number here is verified against school-wise attendance records and session reports.</p>
    <div class="mosaic reveal">
      <div class="mtile m-red"><b data-count="44">0</b><div class="lbl">Schools Implemented</div><p>Government UP &amp; high schools across four districts, each running the full 30-session curriculum.</p></div>
      <div class="mtile m-ink"><b data-count="1300" data-suffix="+">0</b><div class="lbl">Students = Families Reached</div><p>Grades 6 &amp; 7, selected from cohorts of 300–400 applicants per school, in rural &amp; coastal Kerala.</p></div>
      <div class="mtile m-cream"><b data-count="4">0</b><div class="lbl">Districts Reached</div><p>Kozhikode, Malappuram, Kannur &amp; Wayanad, across four phases.</p></div>
      <div class="mtile m-bordered"><b data-count="14">0</b><div class="lbl">→ Students at Zero2Entrepreneur Bootcamp</div><p>Selected for the Zero2Entrepreneur Bootcamp, part of the TechTop 2025 International Inclusive Innovation Challenge, 28 Nov–4 Dec 2025, Maker Village, Kochi — run by TechTop with partner sponsors, a national platform (Manorama Online, Dec 2025).</p></div>
      <div class="m-photo reveal"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/robot-track.jpg" alt="Student-built robot on test track"></div>
      <div class="mtile m-state"><b data-count="20" data-suffix="+">0</b><div class="lbl">Students with State-Level Recognition</div><p>Won recognition at the innovation competition hosted by Kerala Government's General Education Department.</p></div>
      <div class="mtile m-national"><b data-count="20">0</b><div class="lbl">→ Students at Inspire Manak</div><p>Participated in the Inspire Manak competition — around 20 students from 8 schools across Kozhikode.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p style="text-align:center;color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:.9rem;margin-top:22px"><b style="color:var(--red)">10+ sub-education districts</b> reached across the four.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- REALITY -->
<section class="reality" id="reality">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow reveal">How We Actually Deliver</div>
    <h2 class="h2 reveal">It wasn't smooth. Here's the log.</h2>
    <p class="lead reveal">Anyone can promise delivery. We can show you the outage log and what we did about it, because we tracked it, phase over phase, in the same reports we hand Walkaroo Foundation.</p>
    <div class="rgrid reveal">
      <div class="rcol">
        <h3>What went wrong</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="width:16px;height:16px" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><line x1="15" y1="9" x2="9" y2="15"></line><line x1="9" y1="9" x2="15" y2="15"></line></svg><span>Intermittent power and internet across rural school labs</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="width:16px;height:16px" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><line x1="15" y1="9" x2="9" y2="15"></line><line x1="9" y1="9" x2="15" y2="15"></line></svg><span>Laptops shared 1-to-3 in several schools</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="width:16px;height:16px" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><line x1="15" y1="9" x2="9" y2="15"></line><line x1="9" y1="9" x2="15" y2="15"></line></svg><span>Wi-Fi access windows limiting simulation time</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="width:16px;height:16px" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><line x1="15" y1="9" x2="9" y2="15"></line><line x1="9" y1="9" x2="15" y2="15"></line></svg><span>Driver and hardware-compatibility issues on ageing school systems</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="width:16px;height:16px" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><line x1="15" y1="9" x2="9" y2="15"></line><line x1="9" y1="9" x2="15" y2="15"></line></svg><span>Learning pace variation needing repetition for mastery</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="rcol fix">
        <h3>What we did about it</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="width:16px;height:16px" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"></path><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"></polyline></svg><span>Mobile hotspots and extended Wi-Fi windows on standby</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="width:16px;height:16px" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"></path><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"></polyline></svg><span>Extension boards and systematic driver checks before every session</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="width:16px;height:16px" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"></path><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"></polyline></svg><span>Team laptop-sharing protocols and seat reorganisation</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="width:16px;height:16px" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"></path><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"></polyline></svg><span>Structured buffer sessions and micro-projects to consolidate concepts</span></li>
          <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="width:16px;height:16px" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"></path><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"></polyline></svg><span>Points-based systems to sustain discipline and peer learning</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:24px;color:rgba(255,255,255,.55);font-size:.85rem">Source: internal session &amp; coordinator reports, tracked school-by-school every phase: the same documents we share with Walkaroo Foundation.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- STUDENT PROJECTS -->
<section class="projects">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow reveal">Proof, not promises</div>
    <h2 class="h2 reveal">What 12-year-olds built</h2>
    <p class="lead reveal">Not toy demos: socially relevant prototypes, designed, coded and presented by government school students.</p>
    <div class="cards" id="proj-track">
      <div class="pcard reveal"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/projects/expo-project-3.png" alt="Students presenting the Waste-Collecting River Boat"><div class="body"><span class="chip">Environment</span><h3>Waste-Collecting River Boat</h3><p>An Arduino-based boat using ultrasonic sensors to detect floating waste, DC-motor propellers and a front-mounted collection net, a low-cost answer to river and sea cleaning.</p></div></div>
      <div class="pcard reveal"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/projects/expo-robot.jpg" alt="Students presenting the Medicine Delivery Robot"><div class="body"><span class="chip">Healthcare</span><h3>Medicine Delivery Robot</h3><p>An autonomous assistant designed to support patients and reduce waiting time inside healthcare facilities.</p></div></div>
      <div class="pcard reveal"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/projects/kids-present.jpg" alt="Students demonstrating the Urine Bag Fill Alert"><div class="body"><span class="chip">Healthcare</span><h3>Urine Bag Fill Alert</h3><p>Automatically monitors urine bag levels and alerts hospital staff when full, for timely intervention, better hygiene, real patient impact.</p></div></div>
      <div class="pcard reveal"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/projects/three-wire-detector.jpg" alt="Students presenting the Three-Wire Fault Line Detector"><div class="body"><span class="chip">Electrical Safety</span><h3>Three-Wire Fault Line Detector</h3><p>An Arduino Uno with push buttons and an LCD screen that gives real-time, safe status alerts for each line in a three-wire electrical system.</p></div></div>
      <div class="pcard reveal"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/projects/expo-lifeguard.jpg" alt="Students presenting the Life Guard hydraulic house project"><div class="body"><span class="chip">Flood Safety</span><h3>Life Guard</h3><p>An automatic hydraulic lift that detects rising floodwater and elevates living spaces and beds to protect occupants — an affordable add-on for homes in flood-prone areas.</p></div></div>
      <div class="pcard reveal"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/projects/money-eating-monster.jpg" alt="Students presenting the Money Eating Monster smart piggy bank"><div class="body"><span class="chip">Awareness</span><h3>Money Eating Monster</h3><p>An interactive smart piggy bank: a sensor detects each coin and a servo mechanism makes the monster "eat" it, turning saving into a game for children.</p></div></div>
      <div class="pcard reveal"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/projects/gas-stove.jpg" alt="Students presenting the Gas Stove Automation System"><div class="body"><span class="chip">Home Safety</span><h3>Gas Stove Automation System</h3><p>A servo-controlled gas knob with ultrasonic boil detection and a smoke sensor that automatically shuts off the stove when unsafe conditions are detected.</p></div></div>
      <div class="pcard reveal"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/projects/smart-gas-detection.jpg" alt="Students presenting the Smart Gas Detection System"><div class="body"><span class="chip">Home Safety</span><h3>Smart Gas Detection System</h3><p>An MQ-2 sensor detects gas leaks and automatically opens windows, cuts power via relay, and activates an exhaust fan to clear the space.</p></div></div>
      <div class="pcard reveal"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/projects/aqua-guard.jpg" alt="Students presenting Aqua Guard"><div class="body"><span class="chip">Marine Safety</span><h3>Aqua Guard</h3><p>Real-time passenger counter and weight monitor for small boats; if tilt is detected, motors pump water to the opposite side to restore balance and prevent capsizing.</p></div></div>
      <div class="pcard reveal"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/projects/air-quality-checker.jpg" alt="Students presenting the Air Quality Checker"><div class="body"><span class="chip">Environment</span><h3>Air Quality Checker</h3><p>An MQ135 sensor detects CO₂ and harmful gases in real time, giving homes and schools an affordable way to monitor air quality and protect health.</p></div></div>
      <div class="pcard reveal"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/projects/smart-farming-robot.jpg" alt="Students presenting the Smart Farming Robot"><div class="body"><span class="chip">Agriculture</span><h3>Smart Farming Robot</h3><p>An automated assistant for crop monitoring and irrigation, reducing manual labour and continuous supervision for small-plot farming.</p></div></div>
      <div class="pcard reveal"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/projects/autoshine.jpg" alt="Students presenting AutoShine"><div class="body"><span class="chip">Hygiene</span><h3>AutoShine</h3><p>Ultrasonic sensors detect footwear at an entrance and activate 360-degree rotating brushes for touchless, automatic shoe cleaning.</p></div></div>
      <div class="pcard reveal"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/assets/projects/automatic-seeder.jpg" alt="Students presenting the Automatic Seeder and Tiller"><div class="body"><span class="chip">Agriculture</span><h3>Automatic Seeder and Tiller</h3><p>A battery-powered robot that simultaneously tills soil and sows seeds with uniform spacing, cutting labour costs for small-scale farmers.</p></div></div>
    </div>
